.TH Remove-DockerNetwork 1 "December 2025" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Remove-DockerNetwork \- remove a Docker network and associated artifacts created by New-DockerNetwork
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Remove-DockerNetwork
\fI[--help]\fR <network-name-or-id>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a Docker network and all associated artifacts created by \fBNew-DockerNetwork\fR.
This includes the shim link, udev rules, and Avahi configuration changes made during
network creation.
.PP
The command accepts either a network name or network ID. If an ID is provided, it is
resolved to the network name for consistent output messaging.
.PP
The script performs cleanup in the following order:
.IP 1. 4
Stops all containers currently attached to the network.
.IP 2. 4
Removes the shim link from Avahi's \fIdeny-interfaces\fR in \fB/etc/avahi/avahi-daemon.conf\fR
and restarts the Avahi daemon.
.IP 3. 4
Deletes the udev rules file (e.g., \fB/etc/udev/rules.d/99-<shim>.rules\fR) and reloads
udev rules.
.IP 4. 4
Deletes the shim link interface using \fBip link del\fR.
.IP 5. 4
Removes the Docker network using \fBdocker network rm\fR.
.PP
The shim link name and udev rules file path are retrieved from Docker network labels
(\fBcom.noblefactor.shim-link\fR and \fBcom.noblefactor.udev-rules\fR) that were set
during network creation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show short usage information.
.SH PRIVILEGES AND DEPENDENCIES
The script requires elevated privileges (calls are run via \fBsudo\fR). It assumes the
presence of:

.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocker\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBip\fR (iproute2)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsed\fR (GNU sed on Linux)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsystemctl\fR (for restarting Avahi)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBudevadm\fR (for reloading udev rules)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxargs\fR (for stopping containers)

.SH FILES
.TP
/etc/avahi/avahi-daemon.conf
Avahi daemon configuration; shim link is removed from \fIdeny-interfaces\fR.
.TP
/etc/udev/rules.d/99-<shim>.rules
Udev rules file created by \fBNew-DockerNetwork\fR; deleted during removal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Remove a network by name:
.RS
.nf
  sudo Remove-DockerNetwork homebridge_eth0
.fi
.RE

.TP
Remove a network by ID (from New-DockerNetwork output):
.RS
.nf
  sudo Remove-DockerNetwork 8f3a9b2c1d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success
.TP
1
Error during network removal
.TP
2
Invalid arguments or network does not exist
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR New-DockerNetwork (1),
.BR docker-network-rm (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR ip (8),
.BR avahi-daemon (8)
